<p>Hi,</p>

<p>The batch you built for BACS date <strong><%= @bacs_date %></strong> failed. Nothing was sent to EUSA.</p>

<pre style="background-color: #f7f7f7; padding: 8px; border-radius: 4px; white-space: pre-wrap;"><%= @error_text %></pre>

<p>
  <% if @draft_link.present? %>
    The EUSA draft was made before the failure, so don't build this batch again, or its claims could be
    drafted twice. <%= link_to "Open the draft", @draft_link %> and check it against the errors above before
    you send it.
  <% else %>
    Its claims are still Approved. Fix the problem, then build it again from
    <%= link_to "Build Batch", new_admin_reimbursements_batch_url(cost_centre: @cost_centre.key) %>.
    If this build left a draft in the send mailbox, delete it first so EUSA isn't asked to pay twice.
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>If you can't fix it, forward this email to IT. They get no other report of it.</p>

<p>Best,<br><%= @cost_centre.automated_sign_off %></p>
